Hi all,

I have a phylogeny and 3-D morphometric data. I want to calculate trait disparity (euclidean dist) between sister species PC scores. Is there a function in geomorph that will do this for me or is there another way I should go about doing this in R?

Thanks,
Nick

From uaab55242ff4da6c6 at groups.google.com  Mon Sep 17 00:06:19 2018
From: uaab55242ff4da6c6 at groups.google.com (Mike Collyer)
Date: Mon, 17 Sep 2018 00:06:19 +0000
Subject: Re: [geomorph-r-package] Calculating trait disparity
Message-ID: <4ILX0KbKlIk.S-1jZufzCAAJ@geomorph-r-package.groups.google.com>
In-Reply-To: <4ILX0KbKlIk.sUJIC_KACQAJ@geomorph-r-package.groups.google.com>
References: <4ILX0KbKlIk.sUJIC_KACQAJ@geomorph-r-package.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/geomorph-r-package/c/4ILX0KbKlIk/m/S-1jZufzCAAJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Nick,

In the form of a script,

fit <- procD.pgls(coords ~ 1, phy = myTree, …)
dist(fit$pgls.residuals)

By fitting a model with only an intercept, the distance matrix among species residuals is the same as the distance matrix among species values, after accounting for phylogeny.  If you rather use PC scores than coordinates,

PCA <- prcomp(fit$pgls.residuals)
dist(PCA$x)

You should get comparable results, regardless.

Cheers!
Mike

